      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_1939ccd33b4ba303b700a75054f71c74e7856d782df3a59f628b94eeac88c0e5",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The proof treats Ramachandra's theorem as a reusable module: after recording two corrections to its printed statement, it specializes a specified subscripted R-parameter to 1 in the theorem's second result and applies Holder's inequality to obtain Lemma 11. The specialization removes generality not needed at this point, while Holder changes the imported aggregate control into the form consumed later. This bridge gains modular economy but hides the exact hypotheses and exponent bookkeeping inside an unproved external result; those details and the validity of the corrected statement remain verification burdens for the scan and cited source.",
